<attribute name="mainDescription" nodeId="eb22cad7">&lt;p&gt;
    An effective way of building Benefits Dependency Maps (also called Benefits Dependency Network) is with colored card or
    Post-it&amp;#174; notes on a large piece of paper on a wall, links and dependencies can then be drawn between enablers and
    benefits. Benefit maps can be developed in one of two ways:
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    &lt;em&gt;Left to right:&lt;/em&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div style=&quot;MARGIN-LEFT: 2em&quot;&gt;
    &lt;ul&gt;
        &lt;li&gt;
            Start with capabilities or process changes being implemented.
        &lt;/li&gt;
        &lt;li&gt;
            Working with relevant stakeholders, identify the required changes that are needed to enable the capabilities to
            work effectively.
        &lt;/li&gt;
        &lt;li&gt;
            Identify what benefits and objectives will be realized from these capabilities and changes.
        &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    &lt;em&gt;Right to left:&lt;/em&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div style=&quot;MARGIN-LEFT: 2em&quot;&gt;
    &lt;ul&gt;
        &lt;li&gt;
            Define the intended strategic objectives.
        &lt;/li&gt;
        &lt;li&gt;
            Identify the key benefits that are required to enable the objective.
        &lt;/li&gt;
        &lt;li&gt;
            Review existing processes and ways of working to identify the changes and enablers that are required to deliver
            the benefits. This process is continued until the key solution components are identified.
        &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    A sample Benefits Dependency Map is shown below:
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    &lt;img alt=&quot;&quot; src=&quot;./../../../core.bus.common.base/guidances/guidelines/./resources/Example_CompletedBDM.jpg&quot; width=&quot;800&quot; height=&quot;400&quot; /&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    &lt;i&gt;Source:&lt;/i&gt; Foreman, Angus, David Howe, and Ulrich Homann. &quot;Software to Services - A Journey by Microsoft.&quot;.
    Microsoft, 22 Aug. 2011. Web. 24 June 2014.
&lt;/p&gt;</attribute>
